       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema can also occur, and the effects can last a long time because of the drug's long half-life.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose. Usual dosing starts at 2.5\u20135 mg daily and titrates up.\n- **Enter a different dose** that you choose, up to 10 mg daily.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 5 mg, I can enter that.\n\nIf you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide is the usual approach. That decision belongs to the prescriber and pharmacy.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
